    "updated_at": "2020-12-29T19:57:50Z",
    "body": "I think they shouldn't be identical, assuming inputs A and B are in the same input report. In the first case you'll have something like:\r\n\r\n```\r\nlet collections = {\r\n  inputReports: [{\r\n    reportId: /*reportID*/,\r\n    items: [\r\n      /*item for input A*/,\r\n      /*item for input B*/,\r\n    ],\r\n  }],\r\n  children: [{\r\n    inputReports: [{\r\n      reportId: /*report ID*/,\r\n      items: [/*item for input B*/],\r\n    }],\r\n  }],\r\n};\r\n```\r\n\r\nFor the second case, inputs A and B should be swapped in the top-level collection:\r\n\r\n```\r\nlet collections = {\r\n  inputReports: [{\r\n    reportId: /*reportID*/,\r\n    items: [\r\n      /*item for input B*/,\r\n      /*item for input A*/,\r\n    ],\r\n  }],\r\n  children: [{\r\n    inputReports: [{\r\n      reportId: /*report ID*/,\r\n      items: [/*item for input B*/],\r\n    }],\r\n  }],\r\n};\r\n```\r\n\r\nParent collections should contain all the items from child collections, bubbled up in the same order they were encountered in the HID report descriptor.",
