    "updated_at": "2020-12-29T21:37:24Z",
    "body": "> Parent collections should contain all the items from child collections, bubbled up in the same order they were encountered in the HID report descriptor.\r\n\r\n:+1:\r\n\r\nI guess the only downside would be if you were to use the inner collections it would be difficult to figure out the data offset for the items, unless you have referential equality on the items and their parent collections.",
